  "behavioral_change": "scipy v_old 1.9.3 to v_new 1.11.4. The keepdims default of scipy.stats.mode flipped, so the mode computed by SMOTEN over categorical neighbors silently loses one dimension.",
  "downstream_effect": "The failure appears as scikit-learn check_array raising 'Expected 2D array', far from the mode call.",
  "reference_fix": "Adds a new `imblearn/utils/fixes.py` defining `_mode(a, axis=0)` that calls `scipy.stats.mode(a, axis=axis, keepdims=True)` on SciPy >= 1.9.0 and `scipy.stats.mode(a, axis=axis)` otherwise, and replaces the direct `scipy.stats.mode` calls with `_mode` in `imblearn/over_sampling/_smote/base.py`, `imblearn/under_sampling/_prototype_selection/_edited_nearest_neighbours.py` and `imblearn/under_sampling/_prototype_selection/_neighbourhood_cleaning_rule.py`.",
